  "query_preview": "/THURSDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 315 PM CDT Tue Jul 28 2026\n\nThe threat for thunderstorms persists into Thursday, though \nconfidence in the convection evolution remains low for now. This\nis largely tied to early day convection, and exactly how this \nwill impact destabilization across the area. If adequate \ninstability can develop Thursday afternoon, a threat for \ndamaging winds and perhaps hail will exist across much of \nwestern and north central Nebraska. Trends will continue to be \nmonitored with respect to the severe threat Thursday. \n\nStronger upper high pressure then begins to establish across \nthe Four Corners as we head into this weekend, with flow \nweakening aloft and becoming more northerly. Heights rise aloft \nand the increasing subsidence will bring drier conditions back \nto western and north central Nebraska. Persistent warm advection\nboosts highs back towards the middle 90s by early next week as \nwell. Will especially have to watch an increasing threat for \nfire weather by Sunday and Monday, when low humidity overlaps \nstrengthening southerly winds.",
